    "turn_text": "and lived there until I went off to college. It's a great place to grow up. I come from a farming family by background. My mom's whole side of the family are farmers, corn, soybeans, wheat, a little bit of Milo, and then I married a ranching girl. My wife, Aaron, is originally from New Mexico. It comes from a ranching family, a cow calf operation out in New Mexico. So she's generation number six, I believe it is, six or seven, born to the ranch. So my boys have, we've got two little boys in almond, so they've got agriculture on both sides of their of their bloodstream. So we hope that they'll have a great love for the outdoors and a great love for agriculture. And it's a great honor for me to get to represent our farmers and ranchers in Missouri here at the United States Center.",
