  {
    "episode_id": 92298,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92298.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's been an interesting few months in Washington. I think you've seen some of the good and also some of the bad in Washington, D.C. I think Congress and the president were able to come together pretty quickly at the beginning of the pandemic. back in March on a very significant relief package that included a lot of help, timely help, to farmers and ranchers in our state and across the country that I think was vital. And I think that was a good strong step that I hope has helped alleviate it, as by no means gotten rid of or obviated the suffering that folks have gone through, but I hope it's made it a little less bad. But, you know, since then you've seen some, I think, of some of the frustrations of D.C. Certainly, I have seen them and that we've not been able to get the Democrats to come with us to get anything more accomplished really in a big way since then. We've been able to do a few fixes here and there, but there's a lot of need out there. We still have folks who want to hire back workers and help and don't have the needs to do",
