    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92298.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. I'm glad you brought up broadband. That's actually one of the things I was hoping to get your thoughts on. I know that you do a lot of work in the technology space as well as broadband. And certainly, as you mentioned, the pandemic has brought to the surface the concerns that we in rural Missouri have known about for a long time with regards to broadband. And I think if there's one good thing that can come out of this entire situation, it's that people are paying more attention to broadband access and availability and what areas in their region may have service and what areas may not. And I think in some cases, that would really surprise some people to learn that. What are your thoughts? I know the Senate and the House are trying to come together on a relief bill. At this point, I'm not sure if we're calling it CARES 2 or Phase 4 or what have you, but There is some talk that there will be some money in there for broadband deployment. I guess any comments you want to make on that whole process. And I will",
