    "turn_text": "That's definitely been a frustration in rural Missouri as well. A lot of the awards that are given out over through the state and federal government quite frankly, they're given out over a long period of time and we certainly appreciate the attention that's being paid but that doesn't help us get broadband in the near future necessarily. So I agree that's something We definitely want to continue to see a dress, and that dovetails right into rural health care. You know, in rural Missouri, we've seen some hospital closures both prior to your time in the Senate and beyond. I would say from a Farm Bureau perspective, as it relates to more non-AG issues, just issues facing rural citizens, I would say healthcare is among the top issues I hear about from our membership when out in the countryside. But telehealth, there's certainly a bright spot there. What are your thoughts on the status of healthcare and where we might be able to go with telehealth if we look at that moving forward?",
