    "turn_text": "Well I think again COVID-19 is really highlighted just how important that these rural service providers for hospitals are for us in Missouri and again for the place around the country and and having grown up in a rural area I can attest to that we had a hospital still due in Lexington where I grew up and and you know it's a lifeline for the community in a very real way. I mean people literally depend on it. and for their end region, which is not just the town, but the entire region. And that's true across our state, whether it's midmo or CMO or Southwest Missouri or Northern Missouri. So this is one of the reasons why I have asked the Secretary of Health and Human Services to prioritize rural hospitals with the money that Congress has appropriated for hospital relief.",
