    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92298.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "I would agree, and I certainly think that healthcare and broadband are two things. As we look forward and we try to think about readiness and preparedness, if God forbid something like this were to happen again in the future, if we invest in these kind of industries and these kind of technologies, at least we'll be better prepared. I mean, we hope that nothing like this happens again, certainly not in the near future. But I think it's important that we take a look at what we've learned and try to invest in technologies and industries that build upon making us more successful. So, Senator, I want to move to trade really quickly. I know that you're certainly very active on foreign policy and with China in particular. I know that you're very active in making sure they're held accountable for various things. But from an agriculture perspective, we really pay a lot of attention to the phase one trade deal with China. I guess just wanted to get your thoughts. Things with China are tense right now, particularly in part because of the pandemic, but there's certainly some other reasons as well. Where do you see that relationship going and what's your take on the phase one trade deal?",
