    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "president would never, just like they said, we could never renegotiate NAFTA and make it any better. And in fact, the president did renegotiate NAFTA. It is better. It is better for Missouri workers. It's better for Missouri farmers and ranchers, Missouri dairy producers. So I think similarly with the phase one deal, is some of the president really had great success in negotiating. Now, here's the key thing, though, is China going to implement it. And that's the big fight now. I think we have got to use every means available to hold China's feet to the fire and make sure that they actually implement this deal they've agreed to. And I have to tell you, already, the president has told me that China is trying to renege on key aspects of the deal. They try to open up a settled portion. The whole deal is settled. According to him, they try to renegotiate portions of it already. That, unfortunately, is pretty much par for the course when it comes to China. They never abide by the deals that they make. And then they try to use the international trade system and groups like the WTO to protect them and to let them wiggle out of these deals. So I think right now, the deal is struck. It is important to our state. We've got to make sure that they actually abide by it. And we need to have every enforcement tool at our disposal and be prepared to use them to see that they abide by it. I will say to Spencer, thinking more broadly, you know, our relationship with China, I suspect it's not going to get any less complicated",
